s="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/diego-portales"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/diego-portales.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Diego Portales</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Diego Portales was a Chilean merchant and minister who dominated the conservative governments of the 1830s.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/diego-rivera"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/diego-rivera.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Diego Rivera</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Diego Rivera was a Mexican painter and a leading figure of the Mexican mural movement.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/diego-rodriguez-porcelos"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/diego-rodriguez-porcelos.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Diego Rodríguez Porcelos</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Diego Rodríguez Porcelos was count of Castile from about 873 to 885, son of Count Rodrigo, under the kings of Asturias.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/diego-silang"><span class="enc-name">Diego Silang</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Diego Silang was the leader of a revolt in the Ilocos region of northern Luzon against Spanish rule during the British occupation of Manila.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/diego-velazquez"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/diego-velazquez.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Diego Velázquez</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Diego Velázquez was a Spanish painter, court painter to Philip IV and a leading artist of the Spanish Golden Age.</span></a></li><li class